From 7bf709d01ad3900edb62a07629acc30af7833746 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:43:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: Every channel of an endpoint has its level; the
 microphone's level and the default format apply.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Sound panel's balance sets the channels of an endpoint apart, as
Windows keeps them: the master volume is the loudest channel's and moves
them all, and the audio clients of every process scale each channel of
what they play by its part (left and right, the centre and the bass
between them). They are kept with the volume in HKCU\Software\Arctic\
Audio.

A microphone's level only muted it: winealsa now scales what it records
by the stream's volumes, and a capture client takes a level changed by
another process as a render client does. Loopback records what an
endpoint plays before its volume.

The default format the panel's Advanced page chooses is the mix format
programs get in shared mode (HKCU\Software\Arctic\Audio\{GUID}\Format);
ALSA's plug converts it for the device.

An endpoint the panel turned off ("Не використовувати цей пристрій") is
DEVICE_STATE_DISABLED, and the name it was given there is its
description, for every program.
---
 dlls/mmdevapi/audiovolume.c      | 112 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 dlls/mmdevapi/client.c           |  44 +++++++++++-
 dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c          |  19 ++++++
 dlls/mmdevapi/mmdevapi_private.h |   2 +
 dlls/winealsa.drv/alsa.c         |   3 +
 5 files changed, 167 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/audiovolume.c b/dlls/mmdevapi/audiovolume.c
